&reftitle.description;
public static Time\DurationTime\Duration::fromHours inthours
Creates a non-negative duration of hours hours. The value is normalized into whole seconds and nanoseconds, see the Time\Duration::$seconds and Time\Duration::$nanoseconds properties.

&reftitle.parameters;
hours
The number of hours. Must be greater than or equal to 0.

&reftitle.errors;



   If hours is negative, a
   ValueError is thrown.


 &ext.datetime.duration-too-long;

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::fromHours example


<?php
var_dump(\Time\Duration::fromHours(24));

try {
    \Time\Duration::fromHours(PHP_INT_MAX);
} catch (\Time\TimeException $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


